# The board's peripheral window sits above the RAM ceiling, so the guest page
# tables map the device gigabyte and codex-vm must back that window with RAM.
# It is per-test rather than global because the window shadows the emulated
# HDA and xHCI BARs, which is what kept these three tests skipped: the flag
# was read as a property of the battery when .vmargs makes it a property of
# the test. Measured 2026-07-27: all three pass with it and are now gated.
-board-mmio